==English==

===Etymology===
< {{etyl|enm}} < {{etyl|fro}} < {{etyl|la}} {{term|malitia||badness, bad quality, ill-will, spite}} < {{term|malus||bad}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-malice.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# Intention to harm or deprive in an illegal or immoral way.  Desire to take pleasure in another's misfortune.
#* '''1981''', [[w:Philip K. Dick|Philip K. Dick]], ''Valis'', ISBN 0-553-20594-3, page 67:
#*: {{...}} not only was there no gratitude (which he could psychologically handle) but downright '''malice''' showed itself instead.

